    "C12N5/06": {
      "code": "C12N5/06",
      "level": 8,
      "parent": "C12N5/00",
      "ja": "｛動物細胞または動物性組織；ヒト細胞またはヒト組織（生体細胞または生体組織の保存Ａ０１Ｎ１／０２）｝<br><br><u>注</u><br><br>このグループにおいては，下記の用語は以下に示す意味で用いられる：<br>全能性細胞は全ての体細胞系（外胚葉，中胚葉，内胚葉），生殖細胞系および胎盤等の胚体外胞組織に分化することができる；<br「分化多能性」細胞は三つの体細胞系（外胚葉，中胚葉，内胚葉）のうちの少なくとも二つの細胞に分化することができる体細胞の幹細胞である；<br>多能性細胞は一つの系のみに限定される。「始原」細胞「前駆」細胞はさらにその系統内に限定される。明白に予見できなければ，全能性細胞は分化多能性細胞に分類される。多能性細胞は分化多能性細胞に分類してはならない。",
      "en": "{Animal cells or tissues; Human cells or tissues (preservation of excised living parts A01N1/10)}<br><br><u>NOTE</u><br><br>In this group, the following words are used with the meanings indicated: <br>a \"totipotent\" cell can differentiate into all somatic lineages (ectoderm, mesoderm, endoderm), the germ line and extra-embryonic tissues such as the placenta; <br>a \"pluripotent\" cell is a somatic stem cell which can differentiate into cells of at least two of the three somatic lineages (ectoderm, mesoderm, endoderm); <br>a \"multipotent\" cell is restricted to one lineage.  \"Progenitor\" and \"precursor\" cells are further restricted within the lineage. If not explicitly forseen, totipotent cells are classified with pluripotent cells. Multipotent cells should not be classified with pluripotent cells. The last place priority rule does not apply between the subgroups of this group",
      "count": 2484,
      "ipcCode": "C12N5/07",
      "coreCode": "C12N5/06",
      "note": "",
      "sourceFile": "cpc_C12N.txt",
      "kind": "cpc"
    },
